	(text "3.3 V always-on, on VSYS_OR after the ideal diode so it rides the hold-up bank with compute. EN tied to VIN. Ship mode removes VSYS. 400 kHz, 3.31 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 358.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "586d9b4b-339b-5f13-bb11-a050ef12537a")
	)
	(text "BUCK12_OFF: pulled down, so a supervisor reset or hang leaves 12 V, compute and the E-stop loop running. Supervisor drives it high in Standby. BUCK24_OFF: pulled up, supervisor drives low to start 24 V.\nThe 12 V converter is the 300 kHz master; SYNCOUT drives the 24 V converter 180 degrees out of phase. 12 V feeds its own VCC through a Schottky after start-up (lower loss)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 340 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "00a83237-e035-5af8-96e9-7da443782580")
	)
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
